 "title": "Risk of a two-asset portfolio",
 "caption": "With two assets of 20% risk and correlation 0.5, mixing them lowers the risk: a 50/50 split has σ = √0.03 ≈ 17.3%, the minimum on this curve. Holding all of either gives 20%.",
 "alt": "A shallow U-shaped curve of portfolio risk against the weight in the first asset, from 20% at 0 and 1 down to 17.3% at 0.5.",
 "description": [
  "With weights w and 1 − w: σp² = 0.04(w² + (1 − w)² + w(1 − w)).",
  "At w = 0.5 this is 0.01 + 0.01 + 0.01 = 0.03.",
  "So σp = √0.03 ≈ 17.3%, below the 20% of either asset."
 ],
